{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1581"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge science/biology","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/science__biology.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",868],["+","The most important excitatory neurotransmitter of the brain is glutamate, the same substance that the kitchen knows as a flavour enhancer: Heinrich Ritthausen first isolated glutamic acid from wheat gluten in 1866, and its salt, monosodium glutamate, gives food the savoury taste called umami. Its main inhibitory counterpart is GABA. "],["=",175]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",802],["+","Der wichtigste erregende Neurotransmitter des Gehirns ist Glutamat, derselbe Stoff, den die Küche als Geschmacksverstärker kennt: Heinrich Ritthausen isolierte die Glutaminsäure 1866 erstmals aus Weizenkleber, und ihr Salz, Mononatriumglutamat, verleiht Speisen den herzhaften Geschmack namens Umami. Sein wichtigster hemmender Gegenspieler ist GABA. "],["=",167]]}]},
